      "AUNT EM: A bad dream?\nAUNT EM: It's past one o'clock in the morning/ Dorothy.\nAUNT EM: Forehead...white. Eyebrows...blue. Nose...crimson. Cheeks...magenta.\nDOROTHY: What's magenta?",
      "DOROTHY: Where is it/ Billina?\nDOROTHY: Billina/ if you don't start laying again/ Aunt Em said she's going to stew you up for supper.\nDOROTHY: • •«oz « «\nAUNT EM: This is just the key to the old house before the tornado. I must have turned it a thousand times.",
      "AUNT EM: Here's your lunch. I was thinking you'd only stay a short time.\nHEAD NURSE: That's not necessary. We have excellent meals here.\nAUNT EM: You must be a good girl and do what the Doctor and Head Nurse . tell you and I'll see you in a week and we'll go home. I've never left her o…",
      "DOROTHY: Will you bring Toto with you when you come to get me?\nAUNT EM: I will. I will do that.",
      "HEAD NURSE: Would you like to go for a ride/ 4 Dorothy? 1\nHEAD NURSE: What did your aunt say?\nNURSE WILSON: Then lie down.\nDOROTHY: Why do you have to tie me down?"
    ]
